      "id": 1,
      "text": "St. Paul was founded in 1854 as a stop on the Texas and Pacific Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Paul%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the first St. Paul’s Church built by settlers in the 1850s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Paul%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "St. Paul’s historic cemetery contains more than 200 graves, many dating back to the town’s earliest days.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.collincountyhistory.com/st-paul.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s Main Street still hosts the 1905 St. Paul Bank building, now a small local history museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.collincountyhistory.com/st-paul.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Every October, St. Paul celebrates its agricultural roots with an annual Harvest Festival on Main Street.",
